# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# 4 · RTI ACQUISITION METHOD
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#   Dual method/technique typing per v1.4 (see changelog §3): the E29
#   procedure (chs:Method / rpm-rti:RTIMethod, linked via chs:useMethod) is
#   complemented by the E55 technique individual rpm-rti:tech-rti (linked
#   via crm:P32_used_general_technique), which is already declared inside
#   rupemagna-rti-1.4.ttl itself and therefore NOT repeated here.

rpm-rti:method-rti
    # acore:Method materialised alongside chs:Method (its declared superclass).
    a owl:NamedIndividual, chs:Method, rpm-rti:RTIMethod, acore:Method ;
    rdfs:label "Reflectance Transformation Imaging (RTI)"@en ;
    dct:description "Photographic RTI acquisition using a custom-built portable hemispherical dome (460 mm diameter, 48 LEDs, 6 tiers). Each session captures 48 sequential exposures under individually activated LEDs for Polynomial Texture Mapping (PTM) and Hemispherical Harmonics (HSH) model generation."@en .
